-- ── DOC-DEVIATION per OWNER-RULINGS R-1/R-1a (binding; quoted verbatim) ──
--
-- Doc §2.3 normative resolution order (rofl-fact-model.md rev 2.0, verbatim):
--   «1. Приоритет автора. Каталог несёт частичный порядок
--       author_priority: Vec<AuthorId> на предикат. Ассершн автора с бо́льшим
--       приоритетом побеждает. Если оба автора вне таблицы или равны — шаг 2.
--    2. Максимальный tick. Более позднее утверждение побеждает. Ничья — шаг 3.
--    3. Минимальный fid. Тотальный, детерминированный, независимый от
--       раскладки, шардирования и порядка сегментов тай-брейк.»
-- i.e. priority → tick → fid.
--
-- AMENDED order per R-1a (OWNER-RULINGS.md, binding; supersedes §2.3 step
-- order): **max tick → author_priority table (optional; empty = skip; seeded
-- with exactly ONE pair: haskell-runtime-globals > haskell-local-refs, living
-- in PredicateDecl.author_priority — the P1 normative field until now consumed
-- by nothing) → author canon-order → min fid.** Grounds in R-1a: (a) semantic
-- correctness decides the measured ties (W23/Q2: prelude's canonical home =
-- runtime-globals / GLOBAL_DEFINITION; EXTERNAL_FUNCTION from
-- __grafema_virtual/haskell-local-refs is the retired representation);
-- (b) zero behavior flip vs storage restored (GLOBAL_DEFINITION 39/39);
-- (c) the one-pair table is not the rejected rot-prone 47-author case, and an
-- EMPTY table degenerates to pure R-1; (d) freshness still dominates — tick is
-- FIRST. PredicateDecl.author_priority is RETAINED and NOW CONSUMED (the
-- seeded pair). Further deviations from the doc's letter, each pre-registered:
--   DEV-1 (emission superset): conflict/5 is emitted on EVERY multi-live
--     resolution — including when tick or the priority table decides — a
--     SUPERSET of §2.3's step-2/3-only emission («когда приоритет автора НЕ
--     разрешил спор»). Nothing is hidden regardless of who wins (R-1a (e)).
--   DEV-2 (predicate column encoding): §2.3's tuple names a PredicateId; §9.2
--     forbids interned u32 ids in canonical artifacts — the conflict tuple
--     carries the canonical predicate NAME as Value::Str. Owner confirm
--     requested; flagged as open question OQ-2.
--   DEV-3 (emission channel): §2.3 says «стор порождает факт … в перспективе
--     audit» (durable audit facts). P5 emits conflict/5 as RETURNED FactKeys
--     (the pinned trait channel, facts/mod.rs:520-526): the store stays
--     monotone, the read path pure. Durable audit-perspective materialization
--     is converter/C7-report policy, NOT P5 (C7's «conflict/5 ≥ 39» is counted
--     from the differential). Owner confirm requested; OQ-4.
--   DEV-4 (Tick column semantics): §2.3 gives conflict(Subject, PredicateId,
--     WinnerFid, LoserFid, Tick) without defining Tick. Minimal call: Tick =
--     the WINNER's tick (snapshot-derivable, deterministic; a wall-clock
--     resolution tick would make read-time emission non-deterministic). OQ-1.

-- ── Pre-registered design decisions E1–E12 ──────────────────────────

-- E1 (the resolution order, k>2 generalization). The R-1a order is implemented
-- as successive FILTERS over the live candidate assertion set (not a pairwise
-- comparator — a pairwise mixed listed/unlisted comparator is not transitive):
--   F1 keep max-tick survivors;
--   F2 (priority table): applies IFF every survivor's author is listed in the
--      decl's author_priority AND not all at one rank — then keep min-rank
--      (rank = index, LOWER index = HIGHER priority); otherwise SKIP (this
--      reproduces the 2-candidate rule exactly: «the table decides ONLY when
--      BOTH authors are listed at different ranks; unlisted-vs-listed,
--      both-unlisted, or same-author = undecided»; no "listed beats everyone"
--      surprise);
--   F3 (author canon-order): keep survivors whose author NAME is minimal in
--      canon Str order — canon = length-then-bytes shortlex (cmp_len_prefixed,
--      derive/canon.rs:163, the Ord-for-Value Str arm :276), NOT plain
--      str::cmp (group_rows' plain na.cmp(nb) at lsm.rs:743 is a different,
--      sort-only order). Direction pinned by the R-1a falsifier: canon-order
--      alone picks haskell-local-refs (len 18 < 23) = EXTERNAL_FUNCTION 39/39;
--   F4 min fid (numeric u128) — unique: survivors here share (tick, author),
--      and same-(fid, author, tick) duplicates are one aid, so fids are
--      distinct ⟹ the order is TOTAL. The read side always decides and NEVER
--      errors: E-FUNC-001 is UNREACHABLE on the read path (pinned by test).
-- The result is a pure function of (snapshot live set, catalog decl, author
-- names): independent of shard layout, segment order, insertion order,
-- assertion-vector order.

-- E2 (Functional scope in P5). Functional = base "node" AND "type" ONLY
-- (tuple (Id(subject), Str(node_type)), lsm.rs:465-477 — subject = c0,
-- value = c1; they cover the entire measured conflict class). "attr"/3 stays
-- MultiValued (deferral recorded above, OQ-5); "edge"/"incoming"/"supersedes"
-- stay MultiValued.

-- E3 (seeding path). with_base_relations() stays UNTOUCHED (base id-space +
-- base_names dispatch are plan-golden-pinned; AuthorId is store-interner-local
-- — the constructor has no author table). LsmFactStore::from_parts
-- (lsm.rs:201-227) interns "haskell-runtime-globals" and "haskell-local-refs"
-- into its AuthorTable, then applies a NEW explicit facts-backend-owned
-- catalog amendment (same ownership precedent as supersedes_decl — catalog.rs
-- «deliberately NOT part of with_base_relations») setting on the "node" AND
-- "type" decls: cardinality = Functional, author_priority =
-- [aid(haskell-runtime-globals), aid(haskell-local-refs)]. Exactly ONE pair,
-- exactly these decls. E-CAT-001 identity subsequently compares against the
-- AMENDED decl; the amend API is not a redeclare and cannot CHANGE a
-- conflicting existing table (idempotent re-amend ok, conflicting re-amend =
-- E-CAT-001).

-- E4 (conflict/5 + audit perspective). from_parts declares the reserved
-- "conflict"/5 decl alongside supersedes_decl (Nary, MultiValued, Timeless,
-- Bool semiring, key (c0), no reverse) and interns the "audit" perspective.
-- Emission = the returned Vec<FactKey>: perspective = audit, predicate =
-- conflict, tuple = [Id(subject), Str(predicate_name), Id(winner_fid),
-- Id(loser_fid), Int(winner_tick)] — one FactKey per LOSER FACT; k live facts
-- → k−1 conflict keys. A winner tick that does not fit i64 is a contractual
-- panic (Int is the §2.3 column type; production ticks are generations ≪ i64).

-- E5 (candidate enumeration — the bounded new primitive). On a pure-v2
-- snapshot the existing keyed reads cannot enumerate candidates (get_node_at
-- returns the first hit only, multi_shard.rs:852-895; find_nodes_at dedups by
-- id): multi_shard gains `node_versions_of_at(snap, id)` — the per-subject
-- analogue of iter_node_versions_at (L0 newest→oldest then L1, tombstone-
-- first, bloom short-circuit, derived columns when the segment carries them,
-- NO newest-wins dedup). Each surviving record projects to its
-- (author = _source, tick = _generation) assertion exactly as the D8 grouped
-- projection does. Reserved "$supersedes" records are excluded. Candidate
-- dedup key = (node_type, source, generation) — the aid identity (fid ⊃
-- value): same-aid re-writes newest-wins (M1 is P7); records differing ONLY
-- in tick or ONLY in value are DISTINCT candidates. The §2.4 killed-aid set
-- (the same one live_filter uses, lsm.rs D14) filters assertions before
-- resolution — resolution reads only LIVE assertions.

-- E6 (E-FUNC-001 exact firing set, from §2.3: «Если ОДИН автор в ОДНОМ батче
-- утверждает два различных значения функционального предиката об одном
-- субъекте — это баг производителя»). Fires IFF one assert_batch contains two
-- Node groups (facts) with equal c0 and UNEQUAL value columns for "node"/
-- "type". Identical-tuple re-assert (same fid) is idempotent — NOT a firing.
-- Abort class = E-MAT-002/E-EXEC-001: pre-commit, WHOLE batch, store unchanged
-- (typed FactStoreError, code "E-FUNC-001", C7 envelope facts/mod.rs:314).
-- Same-author distinct values across DIFFERENT batches at the same tick is
-- NOT E-FUNC-001 — both live, resolved at read (tick tie → priority
-- equal-author skip → canon equal skip → min fid): exactly the case the E8
-- fold-key fix must keep survivable. The read-side arm is unreachable by
-- construction under R-1a totality (E1) — pinned as a test, per the
-- E-FUNC-001 extraction ruling.

-- E7 (resolve on MultiValued). resolve_functional on a MultiValued predicate
-- is a caller contract violation: typed FactStoreError, NEW stable code
-- "E-FUNC-002" (C7 convention; owner ack requested, OQ-3). The blanket
-- E-CAP-001("functional-resolution") stub (lsm.rs:1209-1221) and its pin test
-- (lsm.rs:2264) are REPLACED — this is the round's ONLY intentional
-- pre-existing-test expectation change (pre-registered here).

-- E8 (fold-key fix — in-scope P4 machinery, §3.2 «⊕ применяется ТОЛЬКО внутри
-- одного aid», aid = (fid, author, tick), fid ⊃ value column).
-- merge_node_segments_derived keys its fold map (record.id, AssertIdent
-- {source, rule, tick}) (merge.rs:172,186) — the VALUE column (node_type) is
-- absent, so two v3 records with same (id, author, tick) but different
-- node_type — reachable cross-batch — collapse into one entry and fold_tags
-- ⊕-folds tags across two DISTINCT aids: a latent §3.2/C3 sha-invariance
-- violation. FIX: the value column joins the node fold identity FOR v3
-- (Assertion-ident) RECORDS — key (id, Some(node_type), Assertion{…}); v2
-- (Legacy-ident) records KEEP the record-model per-id collapse (id, None,
-- Legacy). Pre-registered refinement of the phase spec's literal
-- «key becomes (id, node_type, AssertIdent)»: including the value for Legacy
-- records would BREAK the pinned D8/D9 v2 winner-collapse (a v2 duplicate id
-- with two types would stop collapsing — the existing pinned test
-- derived_merge_collapses_v2_records_newest_wins, merge.rs:594, collapses
-- exactly that shape, and v2 Legacy idents all carry tick 0, so the two
-- survivors would order by TYPE, flipping the projection winner and the sha
-- across compaction — a C3 violation the literal reading would introduce).
-- §3.2's aid semantics are ASSERTION semantics; v2 records are the record
-- model by D8. The deterministic output sort (merge.rs:203-208) is extended
-- with the value component so output order stays total. Metadata stays OUT of
-- the fold identity (R-3: meta-only differences remain ONE record).
-- merge_edge_segments_derived needs no change: EdgeKey (src,dst,type) already
-- IS the value tuple (merge.rs:219).
-- E8a (same class, projection layer — required for the C3 gate to be
-- OBSERVABLE at the facts read level): node_candidates' per-id assertion
-- dedup key (source, generation) (lsm.rs:652-657) has the SAME value-omission
-- — two same-(author, tick) different-type v3 records would project only the
-- newest. Its key gains the value column: (node_type, source, generation).
-- edge_candidates needs no change (its map key already carries the full
-- (src, dst, type) value tuple).

-- E9 (supersession interplay, §2.4/§4.2). Resolution reads only LIVE
-- assertions: supersede the loser's assertions → subject becomes single-fact
-- → no conflict emitted; supersede the WINNER's assertions → the former loser
-- is now the sole/winning fact (or resolution re-runs over the remainder).
-- Both directions tested. resolve_functional itself NEVER writes supersedes
-- facts (facts-side-only scope; sha unchanged by resolution reads).

-- E10 (P5-vs-legacy divergence honesty). winner == storage winner is a
-- MEASURED real-base property, not a theorem: a fixture where a LOWER-tick
-- record is written LATER shows resolve_functional (max tick) ≠ get_node_at
-- (newest segment) — pinned explicitly as the documented divergence; legacy
-- unchanged until P6.

-- E11 (test seam for counterfactuals). The winner-selection is factored so the
-- differential can run it with an OVERRIDDEN priority table (empty = pure
-- R-1) without touching the production decl — a #[cfg(test)] seam, not a
-- public API.

-- E12 (the "golden fid vector b0093490018cd3e0" reference). No committed R8a
-- digest artifact exists in the repo (verified: the hex appears only as
-- mod.rs:724 GOLDEN_FID_LE_HEX and its round-007 record). Interpretation
-- taken: the min-fid counterfactual is computed with the fid() layout PINNED
-- by that golden vector (fid_golden_vector_pins_canon_input_layout).
-- round-011 records the measured split and the measured blake3 digest of the
-- sorted min-fid winner vector as the NEW pinned artifact.

-- ── Hypotheses (round-011 verifies each; expected-vs-found) ─────────

-- X1 (THE RE-PINNED REAL-BASE DIFFERENTIAL — the settled ground truth). On
-- /tmp/rofl-p2-real-base (manifest 000171, 503,404 distinct node ids;
-- lsof-checked /tmp copy, /home/dev/grafema never touched):
-- resolve_functional over projected node facts finds EXACTLY 39 multi-live
-- subjects → 39 conflict/5 keys; winner == storage winner (get_node_at
-- physics) == GLOBAL_DEFINITION on ALL 39, decided at the TICK-TIE step by
-- the seeded pair; "node" and "type" resolutions agree. R8a falsifier data
-- re-verified in the same run: generation multiset ('1','1')×39;
-- counterfactual EMPTY-table (pure R-1) resolution → EXTERNAL_FUNCTION 39/39
-- (the documented would-be flip — WHY the pair exists); counterfactual
-- min-fid-only split 20/19 (multiset {20,19}; per-side counts + fid-vector
-- digest recorded per E12). All pre-existing differential digests unchanged;
-- pair2/pair7 shadowed accounting stays the explained-exception frame
-- (pair2 shadowed = 39 on the real base).

-- X2 (totality/determinism). Resolution is total (always Some winner on
-- non-empty live candidates — fid uniqueness) and deterministic under
-- permutation of insertion order, shard count, and assertion order; the
-- read-side E-FUNC-001 arm is unreachable (same test).

-- X3 (step order). (i) max tick dominates the table — a NEWER tick from the
-- LOWER-priority author (haskell-local-refs) wins; (ii) the table decides
-- only on tick ties and only when BOTH authors are listed at different ranks
-- (haskell-runtime-globals beats haskell-local-refs on a tie — against
-- canon-order, which would pick the opposite); (iii) unlisted-vs-listed falls
-- through to canon-order (a short unlisted author beats the listed
-- runtime-globals); (iv) canon-order is SHORTLEX: 'zz' beats 'aaa' (plain
-- lex would pick 'aaa'); (v) min-fid final step: same author, same tick, two
-- values cross-batch → min u128 fid wins, NO error. Empty-table
-- degeneration: priority stripped ⟹ ≡ pure R-1 (tick → canon → fid) on the
-- same fixtures.

-- X4 (conflict/5). 3-live-fact subject → exactly 2 conflict keys; agreement
-- (two authors, same fid) → NO conflict; emission also when tick decides
-- (DEV-1 superset); FactKey shape [Id, Str(name), Id, Id, Int] with
-- perspective = audit pinned; conflict/5 and "audit" declared at
-- construction; the conflict relation READS as an honest empty relation
-- (no durable materialization, DEV-3).

-- X5 (E-FUNC-001 write gate). One batch, one author, two Node groups same id
-- different node_type → whole batch aborts pre-commit with E-FUNC-001, store
-- observably unchanged (sha + counts); identical-tuple re-assert in one
-- batch → idempotent, no error; same-author different-value across two
-- batches → NO error, both live, read-time min-fid resolution (X3-v).

-- X6 (E-FUNC-002). resolve_functional on edge/incoming/attr/supersedes →
-- typed E-FUNC-002 (never panic, never silent None). The E-CAP-001 stub test
-- is replaced (E7 — the round's only pre-existing expectation change).

-- X7 (supersession interplay, E9): both directions; resolve writes nothing
-- (sha byte-identical across resolve calls).

-- X8 (fold-key C3 regression, E8/E8a): two v3 node records same
-- (id, _source, _generation), different node_type, two commits → FullMerge →
-- BOTH survive as distinct live assertions; canonical_state_sha identical
-- before/after compact(); Count-semiring tags NOT ⊕-folded across the two
-- aids; R-3 guard: meta-only difference at same (id, type, aid) still
-- collapses to one record; merge output order deterministic with the
-- extended key; existing edge-merge tests untouched-green; the v2
-- winner-collapse pins (derived_merge_collapses_v2_records_newest_wins and
-- the equivalence pairs) untouched-green.

-- X9 (catalog amendment, E3): from_parts-amended node/type decls carry
-- Functional + the seeded pair; identical re-amend idempotent; conflicting
-- amend → E-CAT-001; the catalog.rs E-CAT-001 identity suite (645-666) stays
-- green against the amended decls; divergence fixture E10 pinned.

-- X10 (regression batteries). P2 12 equivalence pairs + P4 batteries
